    "input_tokens": 7783,
    "output_tokens": 73
   }
  },
  {
   "turn": 6,
   "response_text": "Now I understand. The config has `include_aux_feature: true` with `aux_feature_strength: 0.28`, which adds a derived column that has strong correlation with the label. This is causing the model to achieve higher accuracy than a healthy run without this feature. Let me verify this is the issue by checking what the auxiliary feature is doing:\n\nThe `_derived_column` function creates a column that:\n- Takes the label `y`\n- Creates random noise with disagreement rate `p` (0.28)\n- Returns `abs(y - noise)`\n\nThis creates a feature that is highly predictive of the label, which artificially inflates validation accuracy beyond the healthy range.\n\nLooking back at the config:\n```yaml\ndata:\n  include_aux_feature: true\n  aux_feature_strength: 0.28\n```\n\nThis setting should not be enabled during normal training as it provides leaked information to the model. The validation accuracy of 0.8763-0.8824 is consistently above the healthy range (0.8519-0.8607), which confirms that the auxiliary feature is artificially boosting performance.\n\nLet me verify the final metric to ensure my analysis:",
   "tool_calls": [
    {
     "id": "toolu_01DrHHaitjvPhGceSd9tAWE4",
